      "message": "[CL Review Agent] Awaiting `syntaxLayerPromise` before setting `this.diff \u003d diff` means that if syntax highlighting fails (e.g. worker timeout or crash), the entire diff rendering will be blocked.\n\nPreviously, `this.diff` was set first, so the diff would render even if syntax highlighting failed later.\n\nTo make this resilient, consider awaiting a caught promise so that failures do not block the diff from rendering:\n```typescript\nconst syntaxLayerPromise \u003d this.syntaxLayer.process(diff).catch(e \u003d\u003e {\n  this.reporting.error(\"Syntax highlighting failed\", e);\n});\n...\nawait syntaxLayerPromise;\n```",
