      "message": "[CL Review Agent] Passing `comments` as a reactive property to every `GrDiffRow` means that whenever the comments array changes (e.g., when a draft is saved), every single row will run its `willUpdate` and `render` cycle because the `comments` property reference changes.\n\nFor large diffs with many rows, this can cause rendering overhead. Consider:\n1. Filtering comments at the parent level (`GrDiffSection` or `GrDiffElement`) and only passing the relevant comments to each row.\n2. Or making `comments` a non-reactive property (not decorated with `@property`) and using a setter to manually trigger updates to `@state leftComments/rightComments` only when the filtered comments actually change.",
